          %p as was to be shown.
          %p The standard derivation of Minkowski’s inequality from Hölder’s inequality is nothing more than a very tidied-up rendering of this argument, but without the additional conceptual explanation given here.
          %h3#relation_to_logconvex_functions Relation to Log-convex functions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            be a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+space"} convex space
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/affine+space"} affine space
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/function"} function
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi D
                  %mo →
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %mn ∞
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: D \to (0, \infty)
            is
            %em log-convex
            if its
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logarithm"} logarithm
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi log
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \log(f)
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/convex+function"} convex function
          %p
            Hölder’s inequality is closely related to the notion of log-convexity. On the one hand, we saw that the inequality follows from the convexity of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+function"} exponential function
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              The collection of log-convex positive functions on a convex domain
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              is closed under pointwise multiplication, pointwise addition, and pointwise sups.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              The statement for multiplication is clear since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi log
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mi log
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi log
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \log(f \cdot g) = \log(f) + \log(g)
              and any sum of convex functions is convex.
            %p
              Similarly,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi log
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \log: (0,\infty) \to \mathbb{R}
              is an isomorphism of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partially+ordered+sets"} partially ordered sets
              and so
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi log
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi sup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mi sup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %mi log
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \log (\sup\{f_i\}) = \sup\{\log(f_i)\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i
              is a collection of convex functions on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                      %msub
                        %mi f
                        %mi i
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sup\{f_i\}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y \in D
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo ≥
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a, b \geq 0
              such that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo +
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a + b = 1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi sup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi a
                    %mi sup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                    %mi sup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ;
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sup\{f_i\}(a x + b y) \leq a \sup\{f_i\}(x) + b\sup\{f_i\}(y);
            %p
              letting
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c
              denote the right side, this holds iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi b
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_i(a x + b y) \leq c
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              (by definition of
              = succeed ")." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi sup
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sup
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mi x
                            %mo +
                            %mi b
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %mi b
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mi since
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi i
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi is
                            %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                            %mi convex
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≤
                          %mtd
                            %mi a
                            %mi sup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo +
                            %mi b
                            %mi sup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                            %msub
                              %mi f
                              %mi i
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    f_i(a x + b y) &amp; \leq &amp; a f_i(x) + b f_i(y) &amp; since\; f_i\; is\; convex \\
                    \&amp; \leq &amp; a\sup\{f_i\}(x) + b\sup\{f_i\}(y) &amp;
                    }.
            %p
              Finally, for the sum
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi f
                      %mo +
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f + g
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi log
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo +
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \log(f + g)
              is convex, it suffices to show that
            #eq:sum.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo +
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo (
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi p
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi q
                      %mi y
                      %mo )
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo +
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi p
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo +
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f + g)\left(\frac1{p}x + \frac1{q}y\right) \leq (f+g)(x)^{\frac1{p}} (f+g)(y)^{\frac1{q}}
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p, q \gt 1
              such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi q
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \frac1{p} + \frac1{q} = 1
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi t
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi p
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi u
                    %mo =
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi q
                    %mo ,
                    %mspace{:width => "2em"}
                    %mi v
                    %mo =
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mfrac
                        %mn 1
                        %mi q
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s = f(x)^{\frac1{p}}, \qquad t = g(x)^{\frac1{p}}, \qquad u = f(y)^{\frac1{q}}, \qquad v = g(y)^{\frac1{q}},
            %p
              the right side of
              %a.maruku-eqref{:href => "#eq:sum"} (1)
              is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi s
                        %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi t
                        %mi p
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mi p
                      %mo ⋅
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi u
                        %mi q
                      %mo +
                      %msup
                        %mi v
                        %mi q
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mfrac
                          %mn 1
                          %mi q
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s^p + t^p)^{\frac1{p}} \cdot (u^q + v^q)^{\frac1{q}}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi s
                            %mi u
                            %mo +
                            %mi t
                            %mi v
                          %mtd
                            %mo =
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 1
                                %mi p
                            %mi f
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 1
                                %mi q
                            %mo +
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi x
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 1
                                %mi p
                            %mi g
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi y
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 1
                                %mi q
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≥
                          %mtd
                            %mi f
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 1
                                %mi p
                              %mi x
                              %mo +
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 1
                                %mi q
                              %mi y
                              %mo )
                            %mo +
                            %mi g
                            %mrow
                              %mo (
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 1
                                %mi p
                              %mi x
                              %mo +
                              %mfrac
                                %mn 1
                                %mi q
                              %mi y
                              %mo )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    s u + t v &amp; = &amp; f(x)^{\frac1{p}} f(y)^{\frac1{q}} + g(x)^{\frac1{p}} g(y)^{\frac1{q}} \\
                    \&amp; \geq &amp; f\left(\frac1{p} x + \frac1{q} y\right) + g\left(\frac1{p} x + \frac1{q} y\right)
                    }
            %p
              where the last inequality is by log-convexity of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
          %p
            This last theorem enters into the account of
            %a{:href => "#Artin31"} Artin (1931)
            of the basic theory of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gamma+function"} Gamma function
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gamma+function"} Gamma function
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msubsup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mn 0
                      %mn ∞
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mi x
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi t
                    %mfrac
                      %mrow
                        %mi d
                        %mi t
                      %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(x) = \int_0^\infty t^x e^{-t} \frac{d t}{t}
            %p
              is log-convex over the domain
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo &gt;
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \gt 0
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              The function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ↦
                    %msup
                      %mi t
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mapsto t^{x-1}
              is log-linear, hence log-convex. Hence the integral defining
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(x)
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \gt 0
              is a sup over suitable Riemann sums that are positive-linear combinations of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %munderover
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %mi n
                    %msubsup
                      %mi t
                      %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mi e
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %msub
                          %mi t
                          %mi i
                    %mi Δ
                    %msub
                      %mi t
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sum_{i=1}^n t_i^{x-1} e^{-t_i} \Delta t_i
            %p and these, and together with their sup, are log-convex by the Theorem.
          %p
            The main fact underlying Artin’s 1931 discussion is the
            %a{:href => "Gamma+function#BohrMollerupTheorem"} Bohr-Haagerup theorem
            (
            %a{:href => "#Artin31"}> Artin (1931), Thm. 2.1
            ):
          #CharacterizationOgGamma.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              The
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gamma+function"} Gamma function
              is characterized as the unique function
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Γ
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi ℕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℝ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma: \{x \in \mathbb{R}|\; -x \notin \mathbb{N}\} \to \mathbb{R}
              satisfying the following conditions:
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(1) = 1
                  ,
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mi x
                        %mi Γ
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma(x+1) = x\Gamma(x)
                  ,
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi Γ
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \Gamma
                  is log-convex over
                  = succeed "." do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mn 0
                          %mo ,
                          %mn ∞
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0, \infty)
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Artin31
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emil+Artin"}> Emil Artin
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Einführung in die Theorie der Gammafunktion
              %p l. Heft, Verlag B. G. Teubner, Leipzig (1931)
              %p
                English translation by Michael Butler:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Gamma Function
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Artin-TheGammaFunction.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
